#{[17592186609821 "Let $f$ be the Boolean function of two variables defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{ }f({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=({x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{x}_{2})\\,\\text{mod}\\,2.\n$$\n\nComplete the following table corresponding to $f.$\n\n| ${x}_{1}$ | ${x}_{2}$ | $f$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n\nHint: If $x$ is an integer, then\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186609844 "Let $f$ and $g$ be Boolean functions of two variables defined as\n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\,\\text{mod}\\,2,\\,g({x}_{1},{x}_{2})={x}_{1}^{{x}_{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nComplete the following table corresponding to the function $g(f({x}_{1},{x}_{2}),{x}_{2}).$\n\n| ${x}_{1}$ | ${x}_{2}$ | $g(f({x}_{1},{x}_{2}),{x}_{2})$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nHint: If $x$ is an integer, then\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186609861 "Given that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is defined by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5,\\,1\\le n\\le 20 \\\\ 0,\\,n\\ge 21,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ndoes $$\n\\displaystyle {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\n$$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?"] [17592186609872 "Let $f$ be the Boolean function of one variable defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{ }f(x)=(x+1)\\,\\text{mod}\\,2.\n$$\n\nComplete the following table corresponding to $f.$\n\n| $x$ | $f$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n\nHint: If $x$ is an integer, then\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186609876 "Consider the following Boolean function:\n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=1-max\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following boolean functions are equivalent to $f?$\n\nI. ${g}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=min\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\}$\n\nII. ${g}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\,\\text{mod}\\,2$\n\nIII. ${g}_{3}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=min\\{1-{x}_{1},1-{x}_{2}\\}$\n\n*Hint: If $x$ is an integer, then*\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186609892 "Consider the following Boolean function:\n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\,\\text{mod}\\,2.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following boolean functions are equivalent to $f?$\n\nI. ${g}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=min\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\}$\n\nII. ${g}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})={x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$\n\nIII. ${g}_{3}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=(1-{x}_{1})\\cdot {x}_{2}+(1-{x}_{2})\\cdot {x}_{1}$\n\n*Hint: If $x$ is an integer, then*\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186609901 "Consider the following Boolean function:\n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=(1-{x}_{1})\\cdot (1-{x}_{2}).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following boolean functions are equivalent to $f?$\n\nI. ${g}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=1-max\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\}$\n\nII. ${g}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\,\\text{mod}\\,2$\n\nIII. ${g}_{3}({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=max\\{1-{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\}$\n\n*Hint: If $x$ is an integer, then*\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{mod}\\,2=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is even,} \\\\ 1, & \\,\\,\\text{if }x\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186612424 "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+1 \\\\ y<3x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186612454 "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y<2 \\\\ y\\le -x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186613153 "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & x>1\\,,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$"] [17592186613164 "Let $D=[0,1]\\times [0,2].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-xy}{3},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle g(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-y}{4},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle h(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186613202 "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x<-1 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & -1\\le x<1 \\\\ 2\\,,\\, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$"] [17592186613751 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & -1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $Y.$"] [17592186613800 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $X.$"] [17592186614589 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}(5-x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$"] [17592186614624 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.0265,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 1\\le x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186615380 "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$"] [17592186617001 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"] [17592186618729 "A high school has $400$ students enrolled. Of this student population, $48\\%$ use the school bus. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the population uses the school bus} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,400.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$"] [17592186618765 "A language school has $160$ students enrolled. Of this student population, $15\\%$ are bilingual. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the population is bilingual} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,160.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=1|{X}_{1}=1).$"] [17592186622766 "Which of the following functions are valid probability mass functions?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & x=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & x=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,g(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}, & x=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,h(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186622783 "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0\\,\\text{or}\\,y<1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}(y-1)}{y}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ {F}_{Y}(y), & x>1,\\,y\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 1.$"] [17592186622811 "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{1-x}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,{F}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}, & y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 1.$"] [17592186622818 "Which of the following functions are *not* valid probability mass functions?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,g(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{7}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{7}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,h(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186625561 "Compute $P(X\\ge 8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186625569 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{x+1},\\, & x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186625585 "Compute $P(X\\ge 6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186627715 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"] [17592186628493 "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nI. $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$\n\nII. $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)$\n\nIII. $\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=f(0)$\n\nIV. $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$"] [17592186635493 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(x+y)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind $P(-1\\le X<10).$"] [17592186636450 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}16+3x>31 \\\\ 2-3x\\ge -16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le$\n{{field-3}}."] [17592186636456 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+2\\ge 8 \\\\ 4y-1>-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186636457 "Which number line shows the solution of the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}t-1<-3 \\\\ 7t+6\\ge 20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186636488 "What is the 