ariable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186642342 "Find the $80$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186642358 "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-y},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186644074 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$"] [17592186644081 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y}{(x+1)^{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$"] [17592186644092 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>1,\\,y<0.$"] [17592186644111 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{8}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{5}{8},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$"] [17592186644149 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{64}{9\\,{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$"] [17592186644163 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+1>-3 \\\\ 9z+13\\ge 76\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n$z$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}."] [17592186654247 "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(-1)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+1\\,,\\, & x\\le -3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,,\\, & -3<x\\le 0 \\\\ -3x\\,,\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186654251 "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\,,\\, & x<-2 \\\\ 2\\,,\\, & x\\ge -2\\,,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$"] [17592186654254 "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(1)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x,\\, & x\\le 2 \\\\ 2,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186654268 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{8}, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfind $P(1<X<2).$"] [17592186654276 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-|3x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}h(x),\\, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2},\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$"] [17592186654326 "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(4)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4,\\, & x\\le 2 \\\\ x-1,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186654746 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $X.$"] [17592186654771 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+3{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $X.$"] [17592186656248 "Find $\\lim_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)$ and $\\lim_{x\\to \\,(\\pi /2)^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1 & \\text{ for }\\,x>\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186656870 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}, & \\,-1\\le x\\le 1,-1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(X<Y<\\frac{3}{2}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{6}).$"] [17592186656891 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$"] [17592186656896 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{3}y}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{3}, & 1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2.$"] [17592186656917 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186656922 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}{7}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186656924 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}+y)}{8}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}).$"] [17592186656937 "$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le y,\\,0<y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4}, & 0<y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le y,\\,0<y\\le 2.$"] [17592186656945 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{xy}, & \\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{2},\\,1\\le y\\le e \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le {e}^{2},\\,1\\le y\\le e.$"] [17592186656947 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{4}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186656950 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}, & 0<x<1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}(1-{x}^{2}), & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0<x<1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x.$"] [17592186657439 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,0.5)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4y, & \\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n  \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=0.5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0.5)$ is shown above."] [17592186657444 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{4}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$"] [17592186657448 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0.5)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}+4)}{13}, & \\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0.5]$  given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0.5)$ is shown above."] [17592186657465 "$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{7}, & \\,\\,1\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above."] [17592186657466 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}+x+y}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$"] [17592186657478 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8xy, & \\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{3}, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0<y<1.$"] [17592186657488 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+3y}{6}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+2y}{4}, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$"] [17592186657495 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$"] [17592186657501 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(4{x}^{2}+1)}{7}, & \\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$  given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above."] [17592186657509 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{12}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+3}{4}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$"]}
